  <span lang="EN-GB" class="MsoTocTextSpan" xml:lang="EN-GB"></span><span lang="EN-GB" class="MsoTocTextSpan" xml:lang="EN-GB"><span style="mso-element:field-end"></span></span></a></span></span></p>

<p class="MsoToc1"><span lang="EN-GB" xml:lang="EN-GB"><span style="mso-element:field-end"></span></span><span lang="EN-GB" xml:lang="EN-GB"><o:p class="MsoNormal">&#xA0;</o:p></span></p>
</div><p class="MsoNormal"><br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/></p><div><a name="_1d6fbcbe-58a5-ef32-9e49-e28535e70928" id="_1d6fbcbe-58a5-ef32-9e49-e28535e70928"></a><h1 class="AbstractTitle">I<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Abstract</h1><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_753f5f73-d44b-911e-e810-36e22c0500e5" id="_753f5f73-d44b-911e-e810-36e22c0500e5"></a>This document is OGC Standard that describes an extended internal structure for an image file that requires more than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>). The general structure is similar to the TIFF specification version 6 but it replaces two essential data structures called Image File Header and Image File Directory for new ones that support the necessary longer integer numbers that acts as internal offsets of the file. It also adds 3 new data types for very long integers. It is expected that other OGC standards, such as GeoTIFF, Will depend on this OGC Standard in the near future.</p></div><div class="Section3"><a name="_8492b3f8-ca4d-580b-4cbe-b15a0837eecd" id="_8492b3f8-ca4d-580b-4cbe-b15a0837eecd"></a><h1 class="IntroTitle">II<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Keywords</h1><p class="MsoNormal">The following are keywords to be used by search engines and document catalogues.</p><p class="MsoNormal">ogcdoc, OGC document, TIFF, image format, big file</p></div><p class="MsoNormal"><br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/></p><div><a name="_19b73fe9-64f4-3a74-9d78-33c380731b8a" id="_19b73fe9-64f4-3a74-9d78-33c380731b8a"></a><h1 class="ForewordTitle">III<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Preface</h1><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ee88feee-eafd-2ce5-80bc-371c791e9bef" id="_ee88feee-eafd-2ce5-80bc-371c791e9bef"></a>When the TIFF format was defined back in 1986 the storage capacity of the computers made difficult (or even impossible) for an single file image to be bigger than Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) long. But today capacities makes it viable and if the file can be random accessed in small pieces, could be useful for example in the case of a big remote sensing dataset that is delivered in a single TIFF file.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c287f438-6361-efb7-3702-8d362a59de7a" id="_c287f438-6361-efb7-3702-8d362a59de7a"></a>The basic BigTIFF design was first proposed in 2004 and refined in (<a href="https://www.asmail.be/msg0055453930.html)">this discussion</a> (now only accessible in the web.archive.org) on the Aware Systems (<a href="https://www.awaresystems.be/)">Aware Systems</a> mailing list (now only available in the web.archive.org). Contributors to the design discussion included Lynn Quam, Frank Warmerdam, Chris Cox, Rob Tillaart, Dan Smith, Bob Freisenhahn, Andrey Kiselev, Phillip Crews, and Gerben Vos. The authors thank all those who came before them for creating libtiff and designing the BigTIFF enhancements. The BigTIFF format was proposed in  <a href="https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html">https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html</a>, maintained by Joris Van Damme, and has been stable in recent years (now only accessible in the web.archive.org).</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e084030e-4c65-17ac-ff27-2f0b15f80d8f" id="_e084030e-4c65-17ac-ff27-2f0b15f80d8f"></a>Changes were made by Ole Eichhorn (<a href="mailto:ole.eichhorn@gmail.com">ole.eichhorn@gmail.com</a>) while at (www.aperio.com)[Aperio] (now only accessible in the web.archive.org) and the work was donated as public domain, in gratitude to Sam Leffler, Silicon Graphics, Joris Van Damme, Aware Systems, Frank Warmerdam, Andrey Kisley, Mike Welles, and all who have worked on libtiff over the years to provide support to files bigger than previous limitations. These changes were published on an &#x201C;as is&#x201D; basis and neither Ole Eichhorn nor Aperio made any warranty as to their fitness for any intended use.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8d4b62bb-1a53-8bca-3c50-12e8ecd66599" id="_8d4b62bb-1a53-8bca-3c50-12e8ecd66599"></a>The intention of this Standard is to elevate the work done by all cited previous people to the category of International Standard recognizing and respecting their work. This document is an adaptation of the <a href="https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html">https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html</a> specification to an OGC Standard format following the OGC Modular Specification. It was done with the intention of creating a transcription with no practical modifications, so old BigTIFF implementations would be immediately compatible with this Standard. In the process, the Standard was made partially dependent from the classical TIFF v6 specification. It is expected that next versions of GeoTIFF will support both classical TIFF v6 and BigTIFF overcoming file size limitations.</p><div class="Note"><a name="_12ede555-91d8-4bbf-2e3f-2dd5f4dea079" id="_12ede555-91d8-4bbf-2e3f-2dd5f4dea079"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>Recipients of this Standard are requested to submit, with their comments, notification of any relevant patent claims or other intellectual property rights of which they may be aware that might be infringed by any implementation of the standard set forth in this document, and to provide supporting documentation.</p></div></div><div class="Section3"><a name="_0508107c-ef65-96e3-cc0f-16595c408e2d" id="_0508107c-ef65-96e3-cc0f-16595c408e2d"></a><h1 class="IntroTitle">IV<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Security considerations</h1><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1c045cb2-9145-d656-3496-9f650a25318f" id="_1c045cb2-9145-d656-3496-9f650a25318f"></a>While this Standard upgrades TIFF by accommodating capacity for massive datasets (such as satellite imagery, gigapixel medical pathology slides, and high-fidelity 3D maps) it introduces specific, security vulnerabilities. The following list is not exhaustive but highlights the most critical concerns:</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9925ce4f-74c8-0736-c9fe-54e09009c9aa" id="_9925ce4f-74c8-0736-c9fe-54e09009c9aa"></a>Memory Allocation Bombs (Severe DoS): With BigTIFF&#x2019;s 64-bit fields, a malicious actor can craft an Image File Directory (IFD) tag indicating that an array requires exabytes or petabytes of memory. If a parser software naively executes memory allocation (malloc) based on that 64-bit header value before validating the actual file payload size, it will cause an immediate application crash or severe system-wide memory exhaustion.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_35300e14-8660-d0c5-9ab8-6faa87b47fb7" id="_35300e14-8660-d0c5-9ab8-6faa87b47fb7"></a>64-bit to 32-bit Truncation Vulnerabilities: Legacy applications handle file pathways using 32-bit code. When a modern BigTIFF library passes a 64-bit offset or byte-count pointer to an older code, the upper bits can be truncated. This type mismatch creates scenarios leading to out-of-bounds memory reads or heap corruptions.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6ba21f1e-ff09-3b9a-0a2a-5792726d668f" id="_6ba21f1e-ff09-3b9a-0a2a-5792726d668f"></a>Unchecked Malware Staging &amp; Steganography: Because BigTIFF files easily scale into tens of gigabytes, they are perfect vehicles for data exfiltration or malware storage. Most enterprise antivirus software, firewalls, and email scanners bypass deep content scanning for files exceeding 50 MB to 100 MB to maintain performance. Attackers can embed entire encrypted payloads into obscure 64-bit tag blocks without altering the viewable image, completely avoiding detection.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_fcd67444-f963-6ec5-0eb8-bf0818a6a9d1" id="_fcd67444-f963-6ec5-0eb8-bf0818a6a9d1"></a>Infinite Tiles: BigTIFF heavily relies on tiled structures to read giant images efficiently. A corrupted or malicious file can define millions of deeply nested that may lock up server CPU threads almost indefinitely.</p></div><div class="Section3"><a name="_26db25a4-d4c4-1ec0-c3d3-21199603cd6e" id="_26db25a4-d4c4-1ec0-c3d3-21199603cd6e"></a><h1 class="IntroTitle">V<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Submitting Organizations</h1><p class="MsoNormal">The following organizations submitted this Document to the Open Geospatial Consortium (OGC):</p><div class="ul_wrap"><p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><a name="_3fe77c7e-cf9c-b43a-1e1b-cafa025aebd9" id="_3fe77c7e-cf9c-b43a-1e1b-cafa025aebd9"></a>UAB-CREAF, Geomatys, IGN-F and Michel Leedahl</p></div></div><div class="Section3"><a name="_19d5589d-7cb6-b05b-148e-a2ad6e39d6ac" id="_19d5589d-7cb6-b05b-148e-a2ad6e39d6ac"></a><h1 class="IntroTitle">VI<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Submitters</h1><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6e1b734b-e32c-864b-59a1-81792b76695c" id="_6e1b734b-e32c-864b-59a1-81792b76695c"></a>All questions regarding this submission should be directed to the editor or the submitters:</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_3b0ac6ff-4f0d-0ff8-b465-b2d5be2985b0" id="_3b0ac6ff-4f0d-0ff8-b465-b2d5be2985b0"></a><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><b>Name</b></td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><b>Affiliation</b></td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Joan Maso</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">UAB-CREAF</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Martin Desruisseaux</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Geomatys</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Gilles Cebelieu</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">IGN-F</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Michel Leedahl</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Michel Leedahl</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="MsoNormal">&#xA0;</p></div>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
      <br clear="all" class="section"/>
    </p>
    <div class="WordSection3">
      <div>
        <a name="_11610782-2d18-50b5-3450-10bcfbd3caad" id="_11610782-2d18-50b5-3450-10bcfbd3caad"></a>
        <h1>1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Scope</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_12de91ad-b82a-e876-bc73-19f5ac7452dd" id="_12de91ad-b82a-e876-bc73-19f5ac7452dd"></a>This document is OGC Standard that describes an extended internal structure for a image file that requires more than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>). The general structure is similar to the TIFF specification version 6 but two essential data structures called Image File Header and Image File Directory are replaced by Big File Header and Big Image File Directory to support the necessary longer integer numbers that act as internal offsets of the file. It also adds 3 new extra data types: LONG8 (uint64) SLONG8 (int64) or IFD8 (uint64).</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1d37bd68-65dd-0686-b64c-c719a8ec6f10" id="_1d37bd68-65dd-0686-b64c-c719a8ec6f10"></a>The intention of this Standard is to elevate the work done by the original creators of BigTIFF to the category of International Standard recognizing and respecting their work. Introducing changes in the original work is out of scope of this Standard version.</p>
        <div class="Note">
          <a name="_52146979-b815-1b42-8f68-3da53d2e138d" id="_52146979-b815-1b42-8f68-3da53d2e138d"></a>
          <p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>In this Standard Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) is used instead of the most common Gigabytes (10<sup>9</sup>) because the limit in the file format size is related to internal offsets expressed using 32 bit long integer numbers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a name="_d3cf351c-f67a-fd97-0465-316b826f0ea5" id="_d3cf351c-f67a-fd97-0465-316b826f0ea5"></a>
        <h1>2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Conformance</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_85868bec-290e-608a-d495-f3a2a1f31c32" id="_85868bec-290e-608a-d495-f3a2a1f31c32"></a>This Standard defines a single conformance class</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8e06a550-d1fb-74b0-7249-0ab33a942342" id="_8e06a550-d1fb-74b0-7249-0ab33a942342"></a><b><a href="#BigTIFFRequirements">Clause 8</a></b> (<a href="http://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/req-class-core">http://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/req-class-core</a>)</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bb52e949-e321-741f-13a6-0f4e7fe1f255" id="_bb52e949-e321-741f-13a6-0f4e7fe1f255"></a>This class defines the requirements of the BigTIFF format.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d2aa981f-0ae7-109c-8e96-b1e91084517a" id="_d2aa981f-0ae7-109c-8e96-b1e91084517a"></a>Conformance with this standard shall be checked using all the relevant tests specified in Annex A (normative) of this document. The framework, concepts, and methodology for testing, and the criteria to be achieved to claim conformance are specified in the OGC Compliance Testing Policies and Procedures and the OGC Compliance Testing web site.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_fd12b4d8-88c2-6720-e397-333b92292ec5" id="_fd12b4d8-88c2-6720-e397-333b92292ec5"></a>It is expected that applications implementing the previous proposed BigTIFF specifications will be compatible with this OGC Standard. However, it is recommended that those implementations are also tested for conformance using the tests specified in Annex A (normative) of this OGC Standard in order to be able to declare OGC Compliance.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3aa9d1ec-3724-e8ae-5c14-7fe772655b63" id="_3aa9d1ec-3724-e8ae-5c14-7fe772655b63"></a>In order to conform to this OGC&#xAE; interface standard, a software implementation shall choose to implement:</p>
        <div class="ul_wrap"><p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo2;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><a name="_9723ac23-d927-3af2-926a-c598e7415640" id="_9723ac23-d927-3af2-926a-c598e7415640"></a>The conformance levels specified in Annex A (normative).
</p>
</div>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_08cbd71b-9eb3-7dce-c29b-bbeb5b8bb686" id="_08cbd71b-9eb3-7dce-c29b-bbeb5b8bb686"></a>The single requirements-class and conformance-class described in this Standard are owned by the standard(s) identified.</p>
      </div>
      <div><h1>3<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Normative references</h1>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_49996d2b-65c1-916b-9bbf-42b933aa0025" id="_49996d2b-65c1-916b-9bbf-42b933aa0025"></a>The following documents are referred to in the text in such a way that some or all of their content constitutes requirements of this document. For dated references, only the edition cited applies. For undated references, the latest edition of the referenced document (including any amendments) applies.</p>


<p class="NormRef"><a name="AdobeTIFF6" id="AdobeTIFF6"></a>Adobe Developers Association, TIFF Revision 6.0 Final, June 3, 1992, Adobe Systems Incorporated, <a href="https://www.itu.int/itudoc/itu-t/com16/tiff-fx/docs/tiff6.pdf">https://www.itu.int/itudoc/itu-t/com16/tiff-fx/docs/tiff6.pdf</a>
</p><div class="display Note NormRef"><a name="_39e20f24-6e8b-1d27-64ab-f2b8acc64108" id="_39e20f24-6e8b-1d27-64ab-f2b8acc64108"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>This Standard includes requirements that overwrite some basic data structures specified in Section 2 of the TIFF Revision 6.0. The rest of the TIFF Revision 6.0 is still a normative reference to this Standard.</p></div>


</div>
      <div><a name="_2469c5b2-2b2f-e483-867b-1f7d5c28b0da" id="_2469c5b2-2b2f-e483-867b-1f7d5c28b0da"></a><h1>4<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Terms and definitions</h1>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8c49041f-8363-1e0b-0484-6e1046987489" id="_8c49041f-8363-1e0b-0484-6e1046987489"></a>This document uses the terms defined in <a href="https://portal.ogc.org/public_ogc/directives/directives.php">OGC Policy Directive 49</a>, which is based on the ISO/IEC Directives, Part 2, Rules for the structure and drafting of International Standards. In particular, the word &#x201C;shall&#x201D; (not &#x201C;must&#x201D;) is the verb form used to indicate a requirement to be strictly followed to conform to this document and OGC documents do not use the equivalent phrases in the ISO/IEC Directives, Part 2.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7bbae1f8-9cf5-3d71-b33b-b85f9ba4c251" id="_7bbae1f8-9cf5-3d71-b33b-b85f9ba4c251"></a>This document also uses terms defined in the OGC Standard for Modular specifications (<a href="https://portal.opengeospatial.org/files/?artifact_id=34762">OGC 08-131r3</a>), also known as the &#x2018;ModSpec&#x2019;. The definitions of terms such as standard, specification, requirement, and conformance test are provided in the ModSpec.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_548e409e-2890-5c36-8c0d-528166f290d6" id="_548e409e-2890-5c36-8c0d-528166f290d6"></a>For the purposes of this document, the following additional terms and definitions apply.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3a4cc38f-6614-34f0-6e5b-8831934c33d4" id="_3a4cc38f-6614-34f0-6e5b-8831934c33d4"></a>For the purposes of this document, the following additional terms and definitions apply.</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-big-image-file-directory" id="term-big-image-file-directory"></a>4.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>big image file directory</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_664ff8c8-77a2-c88e-5ce0-e6ebab191e0e" id="_664ff8c8-77a2-c88e-5ce0-e6ebab191e0e"></a>a modified <i>image file directory</i> data structure containing the TIFF fields (identified by a tag) of a BigTIFF file.</p>


<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-big-image-file-header" id="term-big-image-file-header"></a>4.2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>big image file header</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b4c05e4a-a46a-ef22-3dca-b1e235e06a03" id="_b4c05e4a-a46a-ef22-3dca-b1e235e06a03"></a>a modified <i>image file header</i> data structure at the beginning of a BigTIFF file.</p>


<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-big-TIFF-or-BigTIFF" id="term-big-TIFF-or-BigTIFF"></a>4.3<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>big TIFF or BigTIFF</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7089bfc1-5b8a-e240-e6ce-d75ce7aa1d42" id="_7089bfc1-5b8a-e240-e6ce-d75ce7aa1d42"></a>a TIFF file that follows this Standard.</p>


<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-classic-TIFF" id="term-classic-TIFF"></a>4.4<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>classic TIFF</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1150a547-d2a2-48f0-5fc5-ce4d47a03f44" id="_1150a547-d2a2-48f0-5fc5-ce4d47a03f44"></a>a TIFF file that follows the TIFF specification version 6.0.</p>


<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-field" id="term-field"></a>4.5<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>field</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c24938d6-63dc-d4de-a8f8-84c55977805a" id="_c24938d6-63dc-d4de-a8f8-84c55977805a"></a>each entry on a <i>image file directory</i> or a <i>big image file directory</i>. A field is characterized by a tag numerical value and contains or points to the data (source: TIFF specification version 6.0)</p>


 <p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-gibibyte" id="term-gibibyte"></a>4.6<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>gibibyte</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0fa31adc-972d-70b6-7c78-a4d87b539023" id="_0fa31adc-972d-70b6-7c78-a4d87b539023"></a>2<sup>30</sup> bytes (1 073 741 824 bytes)</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c8580896-5da2-8261-ff1d-a73c076cd093" id="_c8580896-5da2-8261-ff1d-a73c076cd093"></a>ISO/IEC 80000-13</p>




 <div class="Note"><a name="_b6ccdb6a-dfca-1de4-a9ca-5ec2777927a5" id="_b6ccdb6a-dfca-1de4-a9ca-5ec2777927a5"></a><p class="Note"><span class="termnote_label">Note 1 to entry: </span>this number is similar but not equal to a gigabyte that is 10^9* bytes (1 000 000 000 or a billion bytes).</p></div>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-image-file-directory" id="term-image-file-directory"></a>4.7<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>image file directory</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2d9c8ce3-80bf-d811-32ba-9254c8f3f2ba" id="_2d9c8ce3-80bf-d811-32ba-9254c8f3f2ba"></a>a data structure containing a list of TIFF fields (identified by a tag) of a <i>classic TIFF</i> file.</p>


 <p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-image-file-header" id="term-image-file-header"></a>4.8<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>image file header</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8d0340f4-768d-8aa4-31cf-54c2186b9053" id="_8d0340f4-768d-8aa4-31cf-54c2186b9053"></a>a data structure at the beginning of a <i>classic TIFF</i> file.</p>


 <p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-offset" id="term-offset"></a>4.9<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>offset</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5ff39eb9-718e-7611-bd4d-fe4edebb825a" id="_5ff39eb9-718e-7611-bd4d-fe4edebb825a"></a>location in bytes with respect to the beginning of the TIFF file. The first byte of the file has an offset of 0.</p>


 <p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-tag" id="term-tag"></a>4.10<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>tag</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_42018cbf-3689-ea63-fed5-3661e01aa04d" id="_42018cbf-3689-ea63-fed5-3661e01aa04d"></a>the identifying number of a field type in the <i>image file directory</i> or the <i>big image file directory</i>.</p>




 <div class="Note"><a name="_3dec64e6-b072-01e6-9c17-1d8c84ad2b5c" id="_3dec64e6-b072-01e6-9c17-1d8c84ad2b5c"></a><p class="Note"><span class="termnote_label">Note 1 to entry: </span>In previous versions of the TIFF specification, the term &#x201C;tag&#x201D; referred both to the identifying number of a TIFF field and to the entire field.</p></div><p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>

<p class="TermNum" style="text-align:left;"><a name="term-TIFF" id="term-TIFF"></a>4.11<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span>&#xA0;<b>TIFF</b></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b5c94703-6ff3-1c99-e182-d6f863986a98" id="_b5c94703-6ff3-1c99-e182-d6f863986a98"></a>a tag-based file format for storing and interchanging raster images</p>


 <p class="MsoNormal">[<b>SOURCE:</b> <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>]</p>
</div>
      <div>
        <a name="_2b3cb9b8-27db-a35e-f4ab-6bdc17e35a7a" id="_2b3cb9b8-27db-a35e-f4ab-6bdc17e35a7a"></a>
        <h1>6<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Conventions</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ffbc3190-3ba5-ecc0-c5b4-9d7891089c97" id="_ffbc3190-3ba5-ecc0-c5b4-9d7891089c97"></a>These sections provide details and examples for any conventions used in this Standard. Examples of conventions are symbols, abbreviations, or special notes regarding how to read the Standard.</p>
        <div><a name="_cb1f7c02-7244-8189-97e4-edcf1570a910" id="_cb1f7c02-7244-8189-97e4-edcf1570a910"></a><h2>6.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Abbreviated terms</h2>

<div align="left"><table class="dl"><a name="_2f7e341c-bd64-4ec5-d6fc-0c3ec610a1c5" id="_2f7e341c-bd64-4ec5-d6fc-0c3ec610a1c5"></a><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">BIFD</p></td><td valign="top"><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_61ea0125-a48e-b379-90d3-ee5337d2e26f" id="_61ea0125-a48e-b379-90d3-ee5337d2e26f"></a>BigTIFF Image File Directory</p>
</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">BIFH</p></td><td valign="top"><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9c9d9002-e625-f4ea-9a0c-94cce6835ec1" id="_9c9d9002-e625-f4ea-9a0c-94cce6835ec1"></a>BigTIFF Image File Header</p>
</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">IFD</p></td><td valign="top"><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c4d0510e-a3ff-8dea-753a-2dd273fa77d5" id="_c4d0510e-a3ff-8dea-753a-2dd273fa77d5"></a>Image File Directory</p>
</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">IFH</p></td><td valign="top"><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_07d7f441-4760-b250-794c-d5e37287dcf5" id="_07d7f441-4760-b250-794c-d5e37287dcf5"></a>Image File Header</p>
</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">TIFF</p></td><td valign="top"><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bf6b4a30-cd9e-3d8f-de8c-190939ea0c15" id="_bf6b4a30-cd9e-3d8f-de8c-190939ea0c15"></a>Tag Image File Format</p>
</td></tr></table></div>
</div>
        <div><a name="_88295426-1be0-25b2-e31d-d04e683c6d66" id="_88295426-1be0-25b2-e31d-d04e683c6d66"></a><h2>6.2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Identifiers</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_06afd127-89ba-2c24-c208-3d8edf1cfc10" id="_06afd127-89ba-2c24-c208-3d8edf1cfc10"></a>The normative provisions in this Standard are denoted by the URI</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7197d0e6-f6c2-b54e-3764-dbccf205caa4" id="_7197d0e6-f6c2-b54e-3764-dbccf205caa4"></a><tt><a href="https://www.opengis.net/spec/bigtiff/1.0">https://www.opengis.net/spec/bigtiff/1.0</a></tt></p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_679bf7bd-7956-7a8a-7d95-1103885c3b33" id="_679bf7bd-7956-7a8a-7d95-1103885c3b33"></a>All requirements and conformance tests that appear in this Standard are denoted by partial URIs which are relative to this base.</p>
</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a name="_ae49ed0a-2085-b204-e829-9ade313be8b6" id="_ae49ed0a-2085-b204-e829-9ade313be8b6"></a>
        <h1>7<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Overview</h1>
        <div><a name="_2bce1848-3e36-bcdb-b85d-cd885a42fbe6" id="_2bce1848-3e36-bcdb-b85d-cd885a42fbe6"></a><h2>7.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>What is BigTIFF</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_cf33e94c-29f0-ab8c-3b07-edcc85b29335" id="_cf33e94c-29f0-ab8c-3b07-edcc85b29335"></a>The TIFF file format was defined in mid-1980s as an extensible format. At that time 32bit offsets seemed sufficient, giving a limit to a 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) file size. This has been quite sufficient for many years. Today however, there is a need for a good multi-purpose open image file format that can handle huge images, or very large collections of images, that together exceed the 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) boundary.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_77636fb2-58fa-ebfd-71d4-b0b54895441a" id="_77636fb2-58fa-ebfd-71d4-b0b54895441a"></a>BigTIFF is very similar to the original TIFF and only changes some internal headers to support 64 bits offsets and data types. The benefits of BigTIFF closely resembling TIFF are huge. For instance, existing TIFF libraries can quite easily extend their support for TIFF to also include this variant. This results in a very short list of requirements. All the much-appreciated properties of the TIFF format that have been around and have been extended for decades are inherited. All properly known tags are being reused, all supported bit depths and datatypes remain valid. The arbitrary number of &#x2018;extra channels&#x2019;, the tiling and striping schemes, the multitude of compression schemes, and the private tag scheme, that made TIFF very useful in pre-press as well as for storing scientific data, and many other applications, all remain intact. Yet, by changing the offset bit depth, BigTIFF files are no longer restrained by the 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) limitation from which classic TIFF suffers.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3d3b5f8c-5ca6-8ada-75b3-fa5f5756c20e" id="_3d3b5f8c-5ca6-8ada-75b3-fa5f5756c20e"></a>Since the BigTIFF format is based on the TIFF format, the reader is encouraged to familiarize with the current version of the TIFF specification before reading this.</p>
</div>
        <div><a name="_cc68f872-21ab-1017-5b7c-0b414e20f8df" id="_cc68f872-21ab-1017-5b7c-0b414e20f8df"></a><h2>7.2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Origin and compatibility</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_48f93b17-4cb2-9aa0-f0ec-cae71775d41e" id="_48f93b17-4cb2-9aa0-f0ec-cae71775d41e"></a>This Standard collects the attempt to launch a new variant of TIFF, called BigTIFF, that closely resembles TIFF, but uses 64bit offsets instead. The results of the BigTIFF discussion resulted in an original specification exposed in the Aware Systems website: <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20240706160214/https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html">https://web.archive.org/web/20240706160214/https://www.awaresystems.be/imaging/tiff/bigtiff.html</a>. Aware Systems was managed by Joris Van Damme but was discontinued after July 6th, 2025 and can only be accessible in backup copies done by the WebAchive iniciative. In order to preserve and consolidate the BigTIFF iniciative, the process of creating this Standard started with Joris Van Damme initial work and was translated it into an OGC standard. Another source of information on the BigTIFF format is the BigTIFF design page at the LibTiff site <a href="http://bigtiff.org/">http://bigtiff.org/</a>.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_65dd7085-7b99-34bb-8175-c23386df74f3" id="_65dd7085-7b99-34bb-8175-c23386df74f3"></a>There are at least two independent implementations of the original BigTIFF specification. (AWare Systems AsTiff, and LibTiff since version 4.0). This OGC Standard does not contradicts the original BigTIFF specification so the implementations of BigTIFF are immediatelly compatible with this Standard.</p>
</div>
        <div><a name="_f313ff6f-3766-26c4-c7b8-76eff5a81db9" id="_f313ff6f-3766-26c4-c7b8-76eff5a81db9"></a><h2>7.3<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Changes to the original version</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b1d48ab8-7749-6a78-f720-9194aed34b17" id="_b1d48ab8-7749-6a78-f720-9194aed34b17"></a>In the elaboration of this Standard a new naming for the data types have been adopted for clarity.</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 1&#xA0;&#x2014; Changes in data types.</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="classic-tiff-file-header" id="classic-tiff-file-header"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Original</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Adopted</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Word</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">unsigned short integer (2 bytes)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Unsigned long</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint32</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">unsigned long integer (4 bytes)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Signed 8Byte</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">int64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">twos-complement signed long long integer (8 bytes)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Unsigned 8Byte</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">uint64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">unsigned long long integer (8 bytes)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
        <div><a name="_b5c378ac-1e31-e021-bd60-7a4153cf0cbf" id="_b5c378ac-1e31-e021-bd60-7a4153cf0cbf"></a><h2>7.4<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Implications for EXIF</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_27459e3e-010a-00e3-6f57-1dfd5863597e" id="_27459e3e-010a-00e3-6f57-1dfd5863597e"></a>EXIF is a metadata standard that uses a TIFF-compatible structure such as <i>image file header</i> and <i>image file directory</i> as a container. It adopts many of the accepted <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> tags and provides an extra list of EXIF tags and a pointer to a dedicated EXIF sub-IFD.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9779a2bc-6cfe-e417-2567-5b1d188c63ee" id="_9779a2bc-6cfe-e417-2567-5b1d188c63ee"></a>EXIF extra tags define a photography-focused subset and extends it with standardized metadata fields for digital cameras. It captures information such as exposure, date/time, GPS, and thumbnail-related data. For TIFF files, EXIF information is integrated by adding new TIFF tags. For the JPEG format, EXIF is included in the Application Market Segment (APP1). APP1 is recorded immediately after the SOI marker indicating the beginning of the file.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_47044b30-0e3a-1261-5876-4bf9b08031e8" id="_47044b30-0e3a-1261-5876-4bf9b08031e8"></a>EXIF specification references Classic TIFF as a data structure and current cameras are not generating images with size bigger that 4Gib. However, nothing prevents a BigTIFF file to use EXIF following the same pattern specified in this Standard (by replacing IFH and IFDs with BIFH and BIFDs respectively). Implementations of EXIF readers should consider the possibility to find BigTIFF structures when reading EXIF, and the need to transform them to Classic TIFF structures when exporting data and metadata to JPEG or other formats.</p><div class="Note"><a name="_2adca713-410c-1d36-b74d-0a9fc3b1b6ae" id="_2adca713-410c-1d36-b74d-0a9fc3b1b6ae"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>In the future, the structure BigTIFF format could support both IFDs and BIFDs and by saving this EXIF part in the first part of the document this issue could be avoided. However introducing changes in the original BigTIFF specification is out of scope of this Standard.</p></div>


</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a name="BigTIFFRequirements" id="BigTIFFRequirements"></a>
        <h1>8<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>BigTIFF requirements</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1cdd1d28-a4df-ab32-5143-6d21f56011b5" id="_1cdd1d28-a4df-ab32-5143-6d21f56011b5"></a>The BigTIFF standard provides a solution for a TIFF file that requires a file size larger than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>). In a BigTIFF file, the largest possible file is 2<sup>64</sup> bytes in length. In this situation the classic TIFF internal 32 bit offsets are not long enough to point to the a byte beyond the 4 Gibibytes limit.</p>
        <div><a name="_a716b5db-5fb6-a715-6ee9-6e739f835fca" id="_a716b5db-5fb6-a715-6ee9-6e739f835fca"></a><h2>8.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Requirement Class Core</h2>

<div class="require"><a name="_529ca719-46b2-41d1-b9ea-5ee7093a7d1b" id="_529ca719-46b2-41d1-b9ea-5ee7093a7d1b"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="req_class_core" id="req_class_core"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Requirements class 1: Requirements Class &#x2018;Core&#x2019;</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/core</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Target type</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">BigTIFF file</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Conformance class</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Conformance class A.1: <tt><a href="#ats_core">https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/conf/core</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Prerequisite</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> (except for the Section 2 that is replaced by the requirements of this Standard)</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Normative statements</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><a><a name="_ccd64992-6a58-4ae6-0c57-ef4e36b96950" id="_ccd64992-6a58-4ae6-0c57-ef4e36b96950"></a></a>Requirement 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_big-offsets">/req/core/big-offsets</a></tt><br/><a><a name="_f9d78cd9-605b-9569-7d2f-cadcd46a7f7b" id="_f9d78cd9-605b-9569-7d2f-cadcd46a7f7b"></a></a>Requirement 2: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_bifh">/req/core/bifh</a></tt><br/><a><a name="_3dc19fa4-d28e-d67c-90ef-3bc8cc5c7053" id="_3dc19fa4-d28e-d67c-90ef-3bc8cc5c7053"></a></a>Requirement 3: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_bifd">/req/core/bifd</a></tt></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div class="Note"><a name="_83773747-2ab3-c6c5-3a5f-74494b1c9158" id="_83773747-2ab3-c6c5-3a5f-74494b1c9158"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE 1:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>This requirement class has <i>BigTIFF file</i> as target of all requirements. Indirectly, the requirements class imposes requirements on a BigTIFF writter (that should deliver a file following these requirements). It also indirectly imposes requirements on how a BigTIFF should operate to understand a BigTIFF file.</p></div>

<div class="permission"><a name="_a4f97272-2366-4a95-af8d-0cba2c87eb91" id="_a4f97272-2366-4a95-af8d-0cba2c87eb91"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="per_class_core_big-offsets" id="per_class_core_big-offsets"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Permission 1</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/per/core/per-big-offsets</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_05d81bd8-8c03-24ac-fb23-2b14589fe58a" id="_05d81bd8-8c03-24ac-fb23-2b14589fe58a"></a>A BigTIFF is allowed to ignore the introduction and the first 2 subsections in Section 2 of the TIFF version 6 specification describing the <i>Image File Header</i> and the <i>Image File directory</i> and use a <i>Big Image File Header</i> and a <i>Big Image File directory</i> instead. When a part of the the <i>Image File directory</i> subsection are still relevant for this standard, it is explicitly reproduced in this Standard</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div class="Note"><a name="_0ed36238-a973-f343-ad11-4b0f1246eb0f" id="_0ed36238-a973-f343-ad11-4b0f1246eb0f"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE 2:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>Commonly &#x201C;permissions&#x201D; are statements that emphasizes the usefulness of some possibilities that may be not obvious, but do not contradict requirements. In this case we are forced to use a permission to overwrite requirements in the original TIFF specification, allowing for 64 bit offsets.</p></div>

<div class="recommend"><a name="_5dc524d4-6b52-42d7-bf34-a32af95fb1fe" id="_5dc524d4-6b52-42d7-bf34-a32af95fb1fe"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="rec_class_core_small-files" id="rec_class_core_small-files"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Recommendation 1</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/rec/core/rec-small-files</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2958fa66-bb3d-c6d8-21e6-17836a0d6005" id="_2958fa66-bb3d-c6d8-21e6-17836a0d6005"></a>In principle, the BigTIFF standard could also support smaller than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) files. However, files that do not require file size bigger than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) or are not using the new data types defined in this Standard SHOULD use Classic TIFF (<a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>) instead of the format defined in this Standard (BigTIFF).</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div class="Note"><a name="_04326c0b-0db0-980e-6495-d07cc7dc762a" id="_04326c0b-0db0-980e-6495-d07cc7dc762a"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE 3:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>This is in order to ensure maximum backwards compatibility with old TIFF implementations not supporting BigTIFF.</p></div>

<div><a name="_e4dae8f5-98db-d85c-259a-8f7dabb97444" id="_e4dae8f5-98db-d85c-259a-8f7dabb97444"></a><h3>8.1.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Basic format</h3>

<div class="require"><a name="_728118be-1572-4d22-aded-5b4d05ae26d3" id="_728118be-1572-4d22-aded-5b4d05ae26d3"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="req_class_core_big-offsets" id="req_class_core_big-offsets"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Requirement 1</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/req/core/big-offsets</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Included in</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirements class 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core">https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/core</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_99dbe6da-24ec-6484-1465-036e385f05fe" id="_99dbe6da-24ec-6484-1465-036e385f05fe"></a>A BigTIFF SHALL shall be a file with a size bigger than 4Gibibytes or a TIFF file using using the new data types defined in this Standard</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">B</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ff707c24-7a1d-be37-b089-9c9c49b587a9" id="_ff707c24-7a1d-be37-b089-9c9c49b587a9"></a>A BigTIFF SHALL begin with a 16 byte <i>big image file header</i> (that replaces the <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> 8 byte <i>image file header</i>)</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">C</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_91316840-0969-ed22-f81a-932e3b1a589b" id="_91316840-0969-ed22-f81a-932e3b1a589b"></a>A <i>big image file header</i> SHALL point to the first <i>big image file directory</i> (BIFD). A <i>big image file directory</i> contains information about the image, as well as pointers to the actual image data in a similar way as a  <i>image file directory</i> does in <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a></p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div class="Note"><a name="_1a3d2215-7931-f795-e864-4fbeba8a9bd7" id="_1a3d2215-7931-f795-e864-4fbeba8a9bd7"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE 1:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>There is a paradox in the actual 4 Gibibytes limit. In a case that all <i>Image File Directories</i> are at the beginning of the file, a 32 bit offset can be sufficient to point to an array of image strips offsets (Tag code 273) and 32 bit numbers may be sufficient for image strips offsets, but imagining that strips are in other and that the second to last strip is at the offset 4.1 10<sup>9</sup> and that the last strip is 250 MegaByte long, the total size of the file will cross the 4 GiB boundary. In a case like this, even if BigTIFF it is not technically necessary, a BigTIFF is mandated by this Standard. This provides a clear criteria to discriminate the need for a BigTIFF file that is independent from order and size of the internal parts of the file.</p></div>

<div class="require"><a name="_d468a933-56e1-4a92-aa69-bbb2ed1b223f" id="_d468a933-56e1-4a92-aa69-bbb2ed1b223f"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="req_class_core_bifh" id="req_class_core_bifh"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Requirement 2</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/req/core/bifh</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Included in</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirements class 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core">https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/core</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_55130143-010d-50d3-3cb7-e2fb8d9de03f" id="_55130143-010d-50d3-3cb7-e2fb8d9de03f"></a>A <i>big image file header</i> SHALL follow the structure presented in <a href="#bigtiff-file-header">Table 2</a></p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 2&#xA0;&#x2014; BigTIFF file header (normative)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="bigtiff-file-header" id="bigtiff-file-header"></a><colgroup><col width="16.6666%"/><col width="16.6666%"/><col width="66.6668%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">Offset </th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="66.6668%">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">0 </th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="66.6668%">Byte order indication (use the values stated in the TIFF version 6 Image File Header Bytes 0-1)</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">2</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="66.6668%">Version number (always 43)</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">4</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="66.6668%">Size of offset in bytes. Always 8 in BigTIFF (it could be 16 in a future version for superbig TIFFs)</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">6</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="16.6666%">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;" width="66.6668%">Reserved. Populate with 0</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;" width="16.6666%">8</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;" width="16.6666%">uint64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;" width="66.6668%">Offset (in bytes) to first BIFD</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3ef6fdb3-7f95-233b-8e21-c7e6c6d270b6" id="_3ef6fdb3-7f95-233b-8e21-c7e6c6d270b6"></a>(The <a href="#annex-classic-tiff-basic-struct-informative">Annex B</a> contains the TIFF version 6 classic structures for comparison purposes).</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ad9a857c-7a9d-df50-3b82-51729b6fcaea" id="_ad9a857c-7a9d-df50-3b82-51729b6fcaea"></a>While the classic TIFF <i>image file header</i> points to the first <i>Image File Directory</i> (IFD), the BigTIFF <i>big image file header</i> points to the first <i>Big Image File Directory</i> (BIFD). In that sense IFD and BIFD are equivalent. Both IFD and BIFD can be located anywhere in the TIFF file. Every &#x2018;page&#x2019; in a multi-page TIFF, either classic TIFF or BigTIFF, is represented by exactly one IFD and one BIFD respectively.</p>

<div class="require"><a name="_8bfb7bae-9c63-4ee8-89e0-1af7c28c6997" id="_8bfb7bae-9c63-4ee8-89e0-1af7c28c6997"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="req_class_core_bifd" id="req_class_core_bifd"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Requirement 3</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/req/core/bifd</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Included in</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirements class 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core">https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/core</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e6e17209-117c-8b8c-f7c7-ed760c8da924" id="_e6e17209-117c-8b8c-f7c7-ed760c8da924"></a>There SHALL be at least ONE <i>big image file directory</i> in a BigTIFF file and each BIFD must have at least one entry</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">B</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2c5f190d-f0f6-85be-481b-4825413c6755" id="_2c5f190d-f0f6-85be-481b-4825413c6755"></a>A BigTIFF file SHALL NOT contain any classic TIFF <i>image file directory</i>. In other words, BIFD and IFD can not be used together in the same TIFF file.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">C</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0ec29c51-c7a7-c9c4-f202-45aeedb81d6f" id="_0ec29c51-c7a7-c9c4-f202-45aeedb81d6f"></a>A <i>big image file directory</i> SHALL follow the structure of <i>Big Directory Entries</i> presented in <a href="#bigtiff-ifd-structure">Table 3</a></p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">D</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e18ef892-eb86-a1f4-c2c5-94c705b0a920" id="_e18ef892-eb86-a1f4-c2c5-94c705b0a920"></a>The <i>big directory entries</i> in a BIFD SHALL be sorted by code (in the same way than classic TIFF requires)</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">E</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_37f226e0-0b80-b577-6474-0174b058797f" id="_37f226e0-0b80-b577-6474-0174b058797f"></a>Each <i>big directory entry</i> SHALL follow the structure presented in <a href="#bigtiff-de-structure">Table 4</a></p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">F</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_aefaab14-898b-0688-841e-3075de1ae5e6" id="_aefaab14-898b-0688-841e-3075de1ae5e6"></a>The tag <i>value</i> SHALL be included inside the tag structure, in the <i>big directory entry</i>, if its size is smaller than or equal to 8 bytes. Otherwise, it SHALL be included elsewhere, and the <i>value</i> SHALL be an offset from the beginning of the file.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">G</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_40345462-3f92-087a-10c7-72aeb17f424f" id="_40345462-3f92-087a-10c7-72aeb17f424f"></a>In case of multibyte values (e.g a SHORT, LONG, etc), the byte order (II or MM) in the TIFF header SHALL govern the order of these bytes.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">H</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bda27bf7-b4ed-776c-e329-b305d4c983b2" id="_bda27bf7-b4ed-776c-e329-b305d4c983b2"></a>The value of <i>Offset to next BIFD</i> in a BIFD SHALL NOT point to a previous BIFD</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">I</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5afbeec3-53e1-0eb0-7964-6812d2fb773c" id="_5afbeec3-53e1-0eb0-7964-6812d2fb773c"></a>The <tt>type</tt> in the BIFD SHALL take priority over the specified (in <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> or elsewhere) <tt>type</tt> of the expected value. In particular, the <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> allows for more than one valid type for some fields. For example, <tt>ImageWidth</tt> and  <tt>ImageLength</tt> are usually specified as having <tt>type</tt> SHORT, but images with more than 64K rows or columns will use the LONG field <tt>type</tt>. The <tt>type</tt> of any specified unsigned integer SHALL be expressed as BYTE, SHORT, LONG or LONG8.</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_95308dcb-03e7-4405-d999-c8a9551dd947" id="_95308dcb-03e7-4405-d999-c8a9551dd947"></a>The last item in the requirement  allows a single procedure to retrieve any integer value, and makes reading more robust, and saves disk space in some situations.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3b27fdd0-2d3b-7c15-894e-bf944a3b2b52" id="_3b27fdd0-2d3b-7c15-894e-bf944a3b2b52"></a>A BIFD consists of an 8-byte count of the number of directory entries (i.e., the number of fields), followed by a sequence of 20-byte field entries, followed by an 8-byte offset of the next BIFD (or 0 if no other BIFD is required).</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d8d221dd-3af4-4d4b-c169-9f7d319c3ad6" id="_d8d221dd-3af4-4d4b-c169-9f7d319c3ad6"></a>Every <i>Big Directory Entry</i> takes up exactly 20 bytes in BigTIFF, and the complete BIFD looks like this:</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 3&#xA0;&#x2014; BigTIFF Image File Directory (BIFD)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="bigtiff-ifd-structure" id="bigtiff-ifd-structure"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Offset </th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">0 </th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Number of big directory entries in BIFD (B)</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">8+0*20</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Big directory entry structure (see <a href="#bigtiff-de-structure">Table 4</a>)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">First tag data in a TIFF field</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">8+1*20</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Big directory entry structure (see <a href="#bigtiff-de-structure">Table 4</a>)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Second tag data in a TIFF field</td></tr><tr><th colspan="3" valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">&#x2026;&#x200B;</th></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">8+(B-1)*20</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Big directory entry structure (see <a href="#bigtiff-de-structure">Table 4</a>)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Last tag data in a TIFF field</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">8+B*20</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">uint64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Offset to next BIFD, if there is a next BIFD or 0 otherwise</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e059e691-0b92-30a4-904e-5ab7ca4678de" id="_e059e691-0b92-30a4-904e-5ab7ca4678de"></a>A <i>TIFF field</i> is a logical entity consisting of TIFF tag and its value. This logical concept is implemented as a <i>Directory Entry</i> in the TIFF version 6 and it is implemented in here as a <i>Big Directory Entry</i>, plus the actual value if it does not fit into the value/offset part, the last 8 bytes of the BIFD Entry.</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 4&#xA0;&#x2014; BigTIFF Tag structure</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="bigtiff-de-structure" id="bigtiff-de-structure"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Offset </th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">0 </th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag identifying code <sup>1</sup></td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype of tag data. See <a href="#datatype-values">Table 5</a></td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">4</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint64</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Number of values (n) (it is not the total number of bytes but the number of values)</td></tr><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">12</th><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">n * Tag data or uint64 offset</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag data (if the size of n * Tag data is lower or equal to 64 bits) or offset to tag data (otherwise)</td></tr><tr><th colspan="3" valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><sup>1</sup> See a list of codes in the TIFF version 6 specification. The GeoTIFF standard adds some extra TIFF tag identifiers.</th></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_df366c58-1048-68e2-5dfb-983a89a1fed8" id="_df366c58-1048-68e2-5dfb-983a89a1fed8"></a>Each <i>TIFF field</i> has an associated <i>Number of values</i> (n). This means that all fields are actually one-dimensional arrays, even though most fields contain only a single value.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6fdbd222-88ae-eb28-5071-34a76736c8b5" id="_6fdbd222-88ae-eb28-5071-34a76736c8b5"></a>The same rule for value &#x2018;inlining&#x2019; the tag data applies to both classic TIFF and BigTIFF, only the threshold size differs. Above the threshold values are pointed by an offset and written elsewhere.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_283e8bc9-a63f-905f-0c66-eab0d65d9bb4" id="_283e8bc9-a63f-905f-0c66-eab0d65d9bb4"></a>Some good practices inherited from TIFF but not specified in <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a> are:</p>

<div class="ul_wrap"><p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><a name="_009f524c-2a33-0e9c-1ff2-f39344af1be8" id="_009f524c-2a33-0e9c-1ff2-f39344af1be8"></a><i>Number of values</i> (n) cannot be zero.
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle"><a name="_409d7665-6e67-0e50-d8ae-c71f7a9947e8" id="_409d7665-6e67-0e50-d8ae-c71f7a9947e8"></a>Offset to tag data in multiple tags cannot be shared (e.g. Tag A and Tag B that not point to the same offset).
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast"><a name="_a5aa5f45-596e-30d8-a712-b7e23409097c" id="_a5aa5f45-596e-30d8-a712-b7e23409097c"></a>Offset to tag data cannot point to the same fragment of the file (e.g. Tag A points to an area of m bytes, Tag B cannot point to part of the same area).
</p>
</div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ceae7897-847a-09bb-658c-6ac9ec8f9740" id="_ceae7897-847a-09bb-658c-6ac9ec8f9740"></a>The following table contains the <i>Tag</i> datatypes that are defined in BigTIFF, in addition to the ones defined in the <a href="#AdobeTIFF6">TIFF&#xA0;Revision&#xA0;6.0&#xA0;Final</a>  (see the last part of <a href="#datatype-values">Table 5</a>)</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table 5&#xA0;&#x2014; BigTIFF Datatype Tag values</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="datatype-values" id="datatype-values"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value </th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Name</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Description</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">LONG8 (uint64)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">64-bit (8-byte) unsigned integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">BigTIFF</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">17</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">SLONG8 (int64)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">64-bit (8-byte) signed integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">BigTIFF</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">18</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">IFD8</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">A uint64 IFD offset</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">BigTIFF</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<div class="permission"><a name="_e1a336af-654a-4fe6-9777-5c19aa18398b" id="_e1a336af-654a-4fe6-9777-5c19aa18398b"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="per_class_core_long8" id="per_class_core_long8"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Permission 2</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/per/core/per-core-long8</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">A</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c8b495d1-fe04-bace-fbd9-b0bba7917e1d" id="_c8b495d1-fe04-bace-fbd9-b0bba7917e1d"></a>StripOffsets, StripByteCounts, TileOffsets, and TileByteCounts tags MAY  have the datatype LONG8 in BigTIFF when necessary. LONG, and SHORT are still valid possibilitities.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">B</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3bf5abf3-e665-f61e-e338-74998333a3b5" id="_3bf5abf3-e665-f61e-e338-74998333a3b5"></a>Tags that point to other IFDs, such as the SubIFDs tag (see TIFF PageMaker version 6), MAY have the datatype IFD8. The datatypes IFD (and the not recommendable LONG) are still valid possibilities.</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div class="Note"><a name="_f0d40704-7ce2-d4db-cd25-2b2e17a7f915" id="_f0d40704-7ce2-d4db-cd25-2b2e17a7f915"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE 2:<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>For future versions it would be useful to add a new datatype &#x201C;UTF8&#x201D;. This will allow for better metadata handling and internationalization.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a name="_bf99a291-81a6-ac6a-16ef-70a61a708381" id="_bf99a291-81a6-ac6a-16ef-70a61a708381"></a>
        <h1>9<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Media Types for any data encoding(s)</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_37d725ed-d0f8-8aac-1eb2-fbebae2b5716" id="_37d725ed-d0f8-8aac-1eb2-fbebae2b5716"></a>IANA defines the image/tiff media type for TIFF (<a href="https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/image/tiff">https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/image/tiff</a>). This Standard suggests the use of the same media type for BigTIFF, since it is a superset of TIFF. As a result, the media type image/tiff is used for both Classic TIFF and BigTIFF files. In principle, clients do not need to negotiate with the servers between classic TIFF or BigTIFF. In fact, this kind of negotiation will enter in contradiction with the first recommendation in this Standards that states that servers and writers should only use BigTIFF for files bigger than 4 Gibibytes (2<sup>32</sup>) or when using the data types introduced in BigTIFF. Old clients not supporting BigTIFF will only receive BigTIFF when Classic TIFF will not work for them anyway. Since a modern software is able to programmatically differentiate between a Classic TIFF and a BigTIFF, they can share the same media time for the BigTIFF.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_756349cc-66e7-8f69-7228-779d12d6d1c0" id="_756349cc-66e7-8f69-7228-779d12d6d1c0"></a>This Standard is also suggesting that same file extension (&#x2019;tif&#x2019; or &#x2018;tiff&#x2019;) is used for both Classic TIF and BigTIFF, despite other previous proposals such as &#x2018;tf8&#x2019; and &#x2018;btf&#x2019; (discussed some time ago in the LibTiff mailing list).</p>
      </div>
      <p class="MsoNormal">
        <br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/>
      </p>
      <div class="Section3">
        <a name="_d415477e-1398-0648-d933-b3b8ed20b283" id="_d415477e-1398-0648-d933-b3b8ed20b283"></a>
        <h1 class="Annex"><b>Annex A</b><br/>(informative)<br/><b>Conformance Class Abstract Test Suite (Normative)</b></h1>
        <p style="display:none;" class="variant-title-toc">Annex A<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Conformance Class Abstract Test Suite (Normative)</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_084b43e1-c795-7d6f-c571-ce140e77d085" id="_084b43e1-c795-7d6f-c571-ce140e77d085"></a>This is the Abstract test of this BigTIFF Standard. However to implement a complete test on a BigTIFF file the dependency on TIFF version 6 should be taken into account. Unfortunately the TIFF version 6 file does not contain an abstract test to guide this developement</p>
        <div><a name="_8002c16f-7fa9-125e-0eb9-b7d3575aa578" id="_8002c16f-7fa9-125e-0eb9-b7d3575aa578"></a><h2>A.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Conformance Class Core</h2>

<div class="require"><a name="_4226c890-642c-410e-8dfb-01655f311506" id="_4226c890-642c-410e-8dfb-01655f311506"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="ats_core" id="ats_core"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Conformance class A.1</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/conf/core</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirements class</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirements class 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core">https://www.opengis.net/spec/BigTIFF/1.0/req/core</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Target Type</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">BigTIFF File</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Conformance tests</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><a><a name="_ed0c90da-81ea-33fe-91d3-102318ddba2b" id="_ed0c90da-81ea-33fe-91d3-102318ddba2b"></a></a>Abstract test A.1: <tt><a href="#ats_core_big-offsets">/conf/core/big-offsets</a></tt><br/><a><a name="_9d480bf6-5c13-40cd-c257-aaf6b42374d4" id="_9d480bf6-5c13-40cd-c257-aaf6b42374d4"></a></a>Abstract test A.2: <tt><a href="#ats_core_bifh">/conf/core/bifh</a></tt><br/><a><a name="_0f270819-86e0-7b7e-b155-2f679f91255c" id="_0f270819-86e0-7b7e-b155-2f679f91255c"></a></a>Abstract test A.3: <tt><a href="#ats_core_api-definition-op">/conf/core/bifd</a></tt></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>

<div><a name="_238a465b-b9ba-8f24-d46b-313dd9c4db69" id="_238a465b-b9ba-8f24-d46b-313dd9c4db69"></a><h3>A.1.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>big-offset</h3>

<div class="require"><a name="_f5e425e2-21d9-4015-af72-a64799fff48d" id="_f5e425e2-21d9-4015-af72-a64799fff48d"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="ats_core_big-offsets" id="ats_core_big-offsets"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTestTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Abstract test A.1</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/conf/core/big-offsets</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirement</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirement 1: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_big-offsets">/req/core/big-offsets</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Test purpose</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_72156a02-8fd3-8589-1e3e-b4925797c8b8" id="_72156a02-8fd3-8589-1e3e-b4925797c8b8"></a>Verify that the section <i>big image file header</i> uses 8 byte offsets</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Test method</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_33aaf943-025e-8cd7-941b-beddc5886cbf" id="_33aaf943-025e-8cd7-941b-beddc5886cbf"></a>Inspect that the BigTIFF begins with a 16 byte <i>big image file header</i> (that replaces the TIFF v6 8 byte <i>image file header</i>). In particular verify that the 2 first bytes correspond to the byte order expected content (0&#xD7;4949 or 0&#xD7;4D4D) and the second 2 bytes represent a 42 or a 43. If it is a 42, consider the file as classic TIFF instead of a BigTIFF.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_961a5f86-9f23-65f3-5816-91e746a39ea5" id="_961a5f86-9f23-65f3-5816-91e746a39ea5"></a>Inspect that the <i>big image file header</i> offset points to an area the content corresponds with a <i>big image file directory</i> (BIFD) structure.</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
</div>

<div><a name="_a04a60de-3119-9f70-724a-bbf6c08fb072" id="_a04a60de-3119-9f70-724a-bbf6c08fb072"></a><h3>A.1.2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>bifh</h3>

<div class="require"><a name="_98349ba9-6a19-4482-ba42-aa764c9ffce0" id="_98349ba9-6a19-4482-ba42-aa764c9ffce0"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="ats_core_bifh" id="ats_core_bifh"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTestTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Abstract test A.2</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><tt>/conf/core/bifh</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirement</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Requirement 2: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_bifh">/req/core/bifh</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Test purpose</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8a8079ef-7ff3-9a88-dcf7-d21ee64aba0c" id="_8a8079ef-7ff3-9a88-dcf7-d21ee64aba0c"></a>Verify that the section <i>big image file header</i> exists and is correctly encoded.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Test method</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_88d493e9-e9bd-f9e4-6f3d-9025c37f5c58" id="_88d493e9-e9bd-f9e4-6f3d-9025c37f5c58"></a>Inspect that a <i>big image file header</i> follows the structure presented in <a href="#bigtiff-file-header">Table 2</a>.</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
</div>

<div><a name="_ba3294ee-dd3b-3ddc-2628-e082dceaded8" id="_ba3294ee-dd3b-3ddc-2628-e082dceaded8"></a><h3>A.1.3<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>bifd</h3>

<div class="require"><a name="_eff57e39-c612-46e9-accc-7522fe0fa34e" id="_eff57e39-c612-46e9-accc-7522fe0fa34e"></a><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="ats_core_api-definition-op" id="ats_core_api-definition-op"></a><thead><tr><th colspan="2" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p class="RecommendationTestTitle" style="page-break-after:avoid">Abstract test A.3</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Identifier</th><td style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;"><tt>/conf/core/bifd</tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Requirement</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Requirement 3: <tt><a href="#req_class_core_bifd">/req/core/bifd</a></tt></td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Test purpose</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b2dc6510-424e-85b1-1955-f218f17c62f0" id="_b2dc6510-424e-85b1-1955-f218f17c62f0"></a>Verify that the section <i>big image file directory</i> exists and is correctly encoded.</p>
</td></tr><tr><th style="font-weight:bold;border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Test method</th><td style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0bb7b8f1-5ff8-2d1f-a267-a301f19ddbcf" id="_0bb7b8f1-5ff8-2d1f-a267-a301f19ddbcf"></a>Inspect that there is at least ONE <i>big image file directory</i> in a TIFF file and that each BIFD have at least one entry.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1dca5cc7-dded-7809-9905-1634bb9e737a" id="_1dca5cc7-dded-7809-9905-1634bb9e737a"></a>Inspect that a classic <i>image file directory</i> is not present in a TIFF file.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d6d588a9-8fa7-0ef9-b2b6-bd2d3bda7eb3" id="_d6d588a9-8fa7-0ef9-b2b6-bd2d3bda7eb3"></a>Inspect that a <i>big image file directory</i> follows the structure of <i>Big Directory Entries</i> presented in <a href="#bigtiff-ifd-structure">Table 3</a>.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c8a49417-c8b9-63e9-a6f1-6608b5864c42" id="_c8a49417-c8b9-63e9-a6f1-6608b5864c42"></a>Inspect that <i>big directory entries</i> in a BIFD are sorted by <i>Tag code</i> (in the same way than classic TIFF does) .</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_333e2f24-b6ce-98cd-c50a-3b75c0cb219e" id="_333e2f24-b6ce-98cd-c50a-3b75c0cb219e"></a>Inspect that each <i>big directory entry</i> follows the structure presented in <a href="#bigtiff-de-structure">Table 4</a>. This can be done by examining the <i>Tag codes</i> and the <i>data types</i> and of the TIFF fields and recognize at least some of them (comparing with tables of accepted values).</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_29a7e482-070b-ce64-87e1-0c54aefa5e0e" id="_29a7e482-070b-ce64-87e1-0c54aefa5e0e"></a>Inspect that the tag <i>value</i> is written inside the tag structure, in the <i>big directory entry</i>, if its size is smaller than or equal to 8 bytes. Otherwise, inspect that it&#x2019;s written elsewhere, and pointed to by an offset written as the <i>value</i>.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e4f13d95-5ea8-03cf-ba6b-d841b69e4f41" id="_e4f13d95-5ea8-03cf-ba6b-d841b69e4f41"></a>In case of multibyte values (e.g a SHORT, LONG, etc), Inspect that the byte order (II or MM) in the TIFF header governs the order of the bytes.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b1bfd6b1-f682-21a1-0baa-d99433c75d32" id="_b1bfd6b1-f682-21a1-0baa-d99433c75d32"></a>Inspect that the value of <i>Offset to next BIFD</i> in a BIFD does not point to a previous BIFD.</p>
<br/><p style="page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b37c3e8b-11cc-2b63-2ff5-0ef6e81f1c62" id="_b37c3e8b-11cc-2b63-2ff5-0ef6e81f1c62"></a>Inspect that the <tt>type</tt> is compatible with the expected value. Since TIFF allows for more than one valid type for some fields, inspect that all types specified as unsigned integer, the <tt>type</tt> is set to BYTE, SHORT, LONG or LONG8.</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
</div>
</div>
      </div>
      <p class="MsoNormal">
        <br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/>
      </p>
      <div class="Section3">
        <a name="annex-classic-tiff-basic-struct-informative" id="annex-classic-tiff-basic-struct-informative"></a>
        <h1 class="Annex"><b>Annex B</b><br/>(informative)<br/><b>Classic TIFF v6 basic data structures and complete list of BigTIFF data types (Informative)</b></h1>
        <p style="display:none;" class="variant-title-toc">Annex B<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Classic TIFF v6 basic data structures and complete list of BigTIFF data types (Informative)</p>
        <div><a name="_b14149e0-7c0f-bd5f-048b-1b2ed5487c87" id="_b14149e0-7c0f-bd5f-048b-1b2ed5487c87"></a><h2>B.1<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Image File Header</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_880c7bdf-a37d-6732-a838-fd2b811ae0e7" id="_880c7bdf-a37d-6732-a838-fd2b811ae0e7"></a>For comparison purposes, we reproduce the original TIFF version 6 TIFF header here.</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table B.1&#xA0;&#x2014; Classic TIFF file header (informative)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="classic-tiff-file-header-annex" id="classic-tiff-file-header-annex"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Offset</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">0</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Byte order indication</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Version number (always 42)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">4</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">uint32</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Offset to first IFD</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
        <div><a name="_8b1e097a-4fdb-eec6-9084-d06f05216081" id="_8b1e097a-4fdb-eec6-9084-d06f05216081"></a><h2>B.2<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Image File Directory</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8ab8d634-e9d4-90e6-910d-a101018966ff" id="_8ab8d634-e9d4-90e6-910d-a101018966ff"></a>For comparison purposes, we reproduce the original TIFF version 6 Image File Directory here.</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table B.2&#xA0;&#x2014; Classic IFD (informative)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="classic-ifd" id="classic-ifd"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Offset</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">0</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Number of tags in IFD (B)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2+0*12</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag structure</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">First tag data</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2+1*12</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag structure</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Second tag data &#x2026;&#x200B;</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2+(B-1)*12</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag structure</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Last tag data</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">2+B*12</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">uint32</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Offset to next IFD, if there is a next IFD or 0 otherwise</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3bc5e5ea-c450-42c1-11e0-4fe6c44c54e4" id="_3bc5e5ea-c450-42c1-11e0-4fe6c44c54e4"></a>Every tag takes up exactly 12 bytes in classic TIFF, and looks like this:</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table B.3&#xA0;&#x2014; Classic Tag structure (informative)</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="classic-tag-structure" id="classic-tag-structure"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Offset</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">0</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Tag identifying code</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">2</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint16</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Datatype of tag data</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">4</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">uint32</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Number of values (n)</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">8</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">n * Tag data or uint32 offset</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;">Tag data (if the size of n * Tag data is lower or equal to 32 bits) or offset to tag data (otherwise)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_a7d54f43-3c29-0b80-9304-ea1b92ad1bea" id="_a7d54f43-3c29-0b80-9304-ea1b92ad1bea"></a>In classic TIFF, the tag data was written inside the tag structure, in the IFD, if its size was smaller than or equal to 4 bytes. Otherwise, it&#x2019;s written elsewhere, and pointed to.</p>

<div class="figure"><a name="img_TIFFandBigTIFFstructure" id="img_TIFFandBigTIFFstructure"></a>

<p class="figure" style="page-break-after:avoid;"><img src="cid:6faffdc0-b218-4b92-8dec-fce312e32b73.png" height="188" width="489"/></p><p class="FigureTitle" style="text-align:center;">Figure B.1&#xA0;&#x2014; TIFF and BigTIFF data structures side by side.</p></div>
</div>
        <div><a name="_2b80851f-a26a-f35a-2916-f4b7f4e95392" id="_2b80851f-a26a-f35a-2916-f4b7f4e95392"></a><h2>B.3<span class="fmt-clause-delim">.</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Datatype Tag values</h2>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d812c7fd-ba52-4862-6229-f3310caa1877" id="_d812c7fd-ba52-4862-6229-f3310caa1877"></a>The following table summarizes the Tag datatypes aplicable for BigTIFF. This list includes &#x201C;Types&#x201D; described in the TIFF version 6 specification, as well as some extra types that have been defined by the BigTIFF (this Standard).</p>

<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table B.4&#xA0;&#x2014; BigTIFF Datatype Tag values</p><div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" width="100%"><a name="datatype-values-annex" id="datatype-values-annex"></a><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Value </th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Name</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Description</th><th valign="middle" align="left" style="font-weight:bold;border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:avoid;">Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">1 </td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">BYTE (uint8)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">8-bit unsigned integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF specification</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">2</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">ASCII</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">8-bit byte that contains a 7-bit ASCII code; the last byte SHALL be a NUL character (binary zero)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF specification</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">3</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SHORT (uint16)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">16-bit (2-byte) unsigned integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF specification</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">4</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">LONG (uint32)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">32-bit (4-byte) unsigned integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF specification</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">5</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">RATIONAL</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Two LONGs: the first represents the numerator of a fraction; the second, the denominator</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF specification</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">6</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SBYTE</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">An 8-bit signed (twos-complement) integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">7</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">UNDEFINED</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">An 8-bit byte that may contain anything, depending on the definition of the field <sup>a</sup></td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">8</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SSHORT (int16)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">A 16-bit (2-byte) signed (twos-complement) integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">9</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SLONG (int32)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">A 32-bit (4-byte) signed (twos-complement) integer.</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">10</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SRATIONAL</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Two SLONGs:  the first represents the numerator of a fraction, the second the denominator</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">11</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">FLOAT</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Single precision (4-byte) IEEE format</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">12</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">DOUBLE</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">Double precision (8-byte) IEEE format</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">13</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">IFD</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">A uint32 IFD offset</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">TIFF PageMaker version 6</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">16<sup>b</sup></td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">LONG8 (uint64)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">64-bit (8-byte) unsigned integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">BigTIFF</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">17</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">SLONG8 (int64)</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">64-bit (8-byte) signed integer</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">BigTIFF</td></tr><tr><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">18</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">IFD8</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">A uint64 IFD offset</td><td valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:auto;">BigTIFF</td></tr><tr><td colspan="4" valign="middle" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><sup>a</sup> It can be used to store a complicated data structure in a single private field, The Count will be the number of bytes required to hold the data structure.  <sup>b</sup> numbers 14 and 15 have   no meaning.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
      </div>
